Subject: [PATCH] pvrsgx 1.17: whitelist B4 SGX530 r1.0.3 HW + ti343x r1.2.1 SW

The early BeagleBoard (Rev A-B4) carries an SGX530 at silicon core revision
1.0.3 (0x10003), read from EUR_CR_CORE_REVISION. The only usable closed
userspace ukernel for this DDK build (TI ti343x) is core revision 1.2.1
(0x10201), so SGXDevInitCompatCheck()'s HW-vs-SW core-revision check fails
with PVRSRV_ERROR_BUILD_MISMATCH and the driver refuses to initialise.

The DDK already ships an exception mechanism for known-good HW/SW rev
mismatches: aui32CoreRevExceptions[], a list of (hw,sw) pairs that set
bCheckCoreRev = IMG_FALSE and skip the fatal check. Add our pair so the
check is skipped for *exactly* this combination -- every other genuine
mismatch still fails. Verified on hardware: full GLES2 offscreen rendering
works on the 1.0.3 silicon with the 1.2.1 ukernel (GL_RENDERER = "PowerVR
SGX 530", correct pixel read-back).

The DDK sources are committed on the OpenPVRSGX linux+pvrsgx branch, so a
plain clone tracks this file; kernel/build-devuan.sh applies the patch with
`patch -p1`.
---
 .../eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
@@ -2692,7 +2692,8 @@
 	const IMG_UINT32 aui32CoreRevExceptions[] =
 	{
-		0x10100, 0x10101
+		0x10100, 0x10101,
+		0x10003, 0x10201  /* B4 SGX530 r1.0.3 HW + ti343x r1.2.1 SW */
 	};
 	const IMG_UINT32	ui32NumCoreExceptions = sizeof(aui32CoreRevExceptions) / (2*sizeof(IMG_UINT32));
